<title>BELGIUM: Belgium bans Cacao Barry buy by Swiss Jacobs unit.</title>
<headline>Belgium bans Cacao Barry buy by Swiss Jacobs unit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's anti-trust authority said on Friday it ruled against the planned takeover by chocolate maker Callebaut AG of French-based cocoa processors Cacao Barry.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the deal would reinforce Callebaut's dominant position and significantly hamper competition.</p>
<p>In Belgium Cacao Barry operates via NV Goemaere.</p>
<p>Cacao Barry is owned by Societe Centrale d'Investissement et Associes (SCIA), which in turn is 51 percent owned by Societe Centrale d'Investissement (SCI) and Belgian holding company Cie Nationale a Portfeuille (CNP).</p>
<p>Callebaut is part of Swiss company Klaus J. Jacobs Holding.</p>
<p>It was not immediately clear whether the ban would affect only the Belgian elements of the merger or block the deal as a whole.</p>
<p>No one was available at the companies for comment.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
